WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:02.880
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.390
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.660
between US and UK Papa John's.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.327
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.050
In the UK, our sizes start at small.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.148
Ours is 9.5 inches across

00:00:18.148 --> 00:00:21.040
with a surface area of 71 square inches.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.510
Joe Avella: Our small pizza
comes in at 10 inches,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.333
which is 78.5 square inches of pizza.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.752
Harry: Next up, we have our medium pizza.

00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:30.350
It's 11.5 inches across

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.543
with a surface area of
103.8 square inches.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.033
Joe: Our large, 14 inches,

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.483
which is 153.9 square inches.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.500
Harry: Finally, for some
reason, we skip extra large

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.350
and go straight to extra-extra large.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.411
This one's 15.5 inches across

00:00:47.411 --> 00:00:51.470
with a surface area of
188.7 square inches.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.020
Joe: We didn't skip the extra large.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.786
16 inches, right here.

00:00:54.786 --> 00:00:57.840
That's 201 square izzos of pizzo.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.680
Our extra large is bigger
than your extra-extra large!

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.347
In your face, Harry.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.277
Harry: In the UK, a small cheese pizza

00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:10.185
will cost you £11.99,

00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:12.430
which is around $15.54.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.800
That's a price per square
inch of 21.8 cents.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.692
Joe: Small in the US, $9.49,

00:01:17.692 --> 00:01:20.500
which is about 12 cents per square inch.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.050
I know I got a small, but
apparently they're also

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:24.710
doing small peppers with the small pizzas.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.430
Look how small this is.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.030
Skimping on the peppers, eh, Papa?

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.820
Harry: An XXL cheese pizza in the UK

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.887
will cost you around $23.32,

00:01:33.887 --> 00:01:37.160
which is a price of 12.3
cents per square inch.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.550
Joe: USA's extra large, $15.49.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.090
That cannot be right.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.520
Sprinkle a little math on that.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.940
That's 7.7 cents per square inch.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.660
That is so cheap.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.230
Harry: So, what can we
take away from this?

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:52.290
Well, in both countries,
the more pizza you buy,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.550
the cheaper it gets.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.530
In the US, the price per
square inch of a small

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.230
is 55% more than an extra large.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:02.293
And in the UK, it shoots
up to a huge 77% more.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.200
Joe: I mean, it makes sense, right?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.040
I mean, that's how they get you.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.740
They pretty much are tricking
you into getting more pizza

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.280
'cause it's cheaper per square inch.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.230
So you're going, "Oh, I'll just get

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.370
the extra large instead."

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.390
And then a year later you're fat. [laughs]

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.340
Whoops. It was such a good deal!

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.210
Harry: It is worth
noting that painful price

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.687
is kind of rare in the UK.

00:02:21.687 --> 00:02:23.427
We got, like, a 40%-off deal

00:02:23.427 --> 00:02:25.070
because we spent a
certain amount of money.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.130
Basically, if you're paying
full price in the UK,

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.040
you're really not getting
the best value for money.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.320
Joe: I'm on their website right now,

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.411
and it looks like, yeah,

00:02:31.411 --> 00:02:34.194
they have endless "specials," or deals,

00:02:34.194 --> 00:02:36.090
for pretty much every
combination you want to get.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.930
Large one-topping pizza, any
two sides, two large pizzas.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.713
I'm assuming what Papa John's does

00:02:41.713 --> 00:02:44.879
is have all types of deals
and codes and promotions

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:47.084
that whatever you get
when you order Papa John's

00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:48.190
was probably a deal for you.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.765
So you probably are
never paying full price.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.210
Harry: In the UK, an
extra-extra-large cheese pizza

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.020
is cut into 12 slices.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.160
Each of these 12 slices is 268 calories,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.993
which brings the total to
a whopping 3,218 calories.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.040
Joe: In the US, our extra
large is cut into 10 slices.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.210
That means each slice
has roughly 300 calories.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.135
And there is no possible way

00:03:14.135 --> 00:03:16.381
you're eating this
pizza without the sauce.

00:03:19.258 --> 00:03:21.520
[hands slapping]

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.610
Whew!

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.600
Harry: What about the most
calorific thing on the menu?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.193
In the UK, it's a sausage
and pepperoni pizza.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.110
Now, for an XXL version of this pizza,

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.930
each slice is 355 calories.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.373
That brings the total to 4,260 calories.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.760
Joe: In the US, if you're
going for most calories,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.460
it's a tie between the meats pizza

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:45.640
and the pepperoni, sausage,
and three cheese pizza.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.300
This used to be John's favorite.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.133
They changed the name.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:49.820
They took his name off of it when he left.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.103
I wonder what happened to that guy?

00:03:52.103 --> 00:03:52.936
[laughs]

00:03:52.936 --> 00:03:56.540
Each pizza is roughly
410 calories per slice.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.560
And since it's 10 slices per pizza,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.740
that is a whopping 4,100
calories per pizza.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.730
Ha!

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.213
Harry: So, despite the average pizza sizes

00:04:05.213 --> 00:04:06.571
being smaller in the UK,

00:04:06.571 --> 00:04:09.040
the pizzas themselves are
actually more calorific.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:09.873
Who knew?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.436
Now, despite Papa John's motto being,

00:04:14.436 --> 00:04:16.011
"Better ingredients. Better pizza,"

00:04:16.011 --> 00:04:17.362
they don't actually make their full

00:04:17.362 --> 00:04:19.530
ingredients list available in the UK.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.858
We did reach out to them to see if they'd

00:04:20.858 --> 00:04:23.070
make an exception for us, but
at the time of shooting this,

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.230
unfortunately we haven't heard back.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.800
Joe: Now, because we can't
get the UK Papa John's

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.407
ingredients list, we're gonna tweak

00:04:29.407 --> 00:04:30.523
this section a little bit.

00:04:30.523 --> 00:04:33.180
We're gonna compare the
US Papa John's ingredients

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:37.750
to another very popular
fast-food pizza chain, Domino's.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.509
Let's get Domino's dough
ingredients on the screen.

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:41.342
[bell dings]

00:04:41.342 --> 00:04:42.830
OK. Now let's compare that

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.555
with the Papa John's US dough ingredients.

00:04:45.555 --> 00:04:48.610
Unbleached enriched wheat
flour, water, sugar,

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.690
soybean oil, salt, yeast.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.140
And that's it.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.710
How hilarious is that?

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:59.180
See? Doesn't need to be
a whole chemistry lab.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:02.230
OK. I gotta give Papa John's
props. That's really great.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.872
They say fresher ingredients,
and they mean it. I like that.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.250
Harry: Here is everything
you can only find

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.240
on the menu at a UK Papa John's.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.260
Joe: And these are all
the USA-exclusive items

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.180
you can get at Papa John's.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.540
Harry: Let's start with the pizzas.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.230
So, in front of me, I have three pizzas.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.057
And across these three,
we've covered pretty much

00:05:20.057 --> 00:05:21.970
all of the items you can
only find on the menu

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.220
at a UK Papa John's.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.690
So, what I have right in front of me here

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.250
is a pizza with a butternut squash base.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.123
Now, this is on the menu as
a gluten-free alternative

00:05:30.123 --> 00:05:31.530
to traditional doughs.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.290
Then the pizzas outside
of that, as you can see,

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.980
have a stuffed crust, which
is just the classic crust

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.390
but then folded over and
filled with a kind of cheesy,

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.300
garlicky mix, which is
really, really good.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.950
Joe: This right here is a pizza consisting

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.580
of only the toppings and crust
that you can get in the US.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:49.370
We have the Parmesan cheese,
garlic-crusted crust.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.532
Crusted crust!

00:05:50.532 --> 00:05:51.540
Harry: Now, from there, you can also

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.070
customize the base sauce.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.930
So instead of the tomato
sauce on this one,

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.240
we have an amarillo chili sauce.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.100
Joe: I was not aware
of this until recently,

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.400
but apparently at a Papa
John's in the United States,

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.550
you can substitute the
tomato sauce for ranch.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.750
And I did exactly that,
because there's nothing

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.020
more American then ranch dressing.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.930
Harry: Papa John's in the UK
actually offers quite a few

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.710
vegetarian and vegan options.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.270
For example, again, on this pizza,

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.090
instead of the classic
mozzarella-blend cheese,

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:22.290
we have a vegan "sheese,"
which is a cheese alternative

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.300
that's friendly for vegans.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.320
So, in the UK, you can top
your pizza with anchovies,

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.480
with tuna, with tandoori
chicken, with spicy beef,

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.727
and also some fake meat alternatives

00:06:32.727 --> 00:06:36.320
such as vegan pepperoni
and also a vegan sausage.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.340
Finally, we have a couple
of vegetarian toppings.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:41.480
For example, on this pizza,
we have some red chilies,

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.870
and on this pizza, we have
feta cheese and sweet corn.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.510
Joe: Cheese. We did do the Parmesan Romano

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.490
and the three-cheese
blend, which is provolone,

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:52.565
fontana, fontania, fontawhatever,

00:06:52.565 --> 00:06:54.335
and Asiago cheeses.

00:06:54.335 --> 00:06:56.302
Salami, Canadian bacon,

00:06:56.302 --> 00:06:58.485
the Philly cheesesteak stuff,

00:06:58.485 --> 00:07:02.440
spinach, and also, of
course, banana peppers.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.070
I don't know what it
is with banana peppers.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.980
They're suddenly on everything.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:07.820
I don't get it.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.585
All right. [sighs]

00:07:09.585 --> 00:07:10.926
Here we go. All right.

00:07:10.926 --> 00:07:13.167
Positive mental attitude. PMA.

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:15.323
I'm about to have the USA Only.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.923
No, I do not like that.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.970
I'll admit it's growing on me.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.950
I wouldn't pick the ranch sauce.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.784
I would stick with tomato.

00:07:35.784 --> 00:07:36.850
But yeah, not bad.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.006
Harry: Oh, God.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.330
That's not good. [laughs]

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.090
Oh, man. Don't, don't order this.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.910
Don't order the UK-only pizza.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:53.560
Moving swiftly on from the UK-only pizza,

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.480
here are some sides you
can only find on the menu

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:56.640
at a UK Papa John's.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.125
We've got some vegan cauliflower wings.

00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:01.020
It's basically just small
pieces of cauliflower

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:02.310
that are breaded and fried,

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.240
and then you can kind of dip
them in a sauce of your choice.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:07.350
Just a nice chicken-wing
alternative for vegetarians.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:09.130
Here we've got some chicken poppers.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.960
Now, I think these are
available in the US,

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.560
but the one that's exclusive to the UK

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.570
is the tandoori chicken spice one,

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.042
which is just pieces of chicken

00:08:16.042 --> 00:08:18.890
breaded and fried with
an Indian spice blend.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.210
Here we've got some tater tots,

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.830
which I'm surprised you
guys can't get in the US,

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:23.997
'cause these aren't
really a thing in the UK,

00:08:23.997 --> 00:08:25.210
but here we can get tater tots.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.210
You can get them with
cheese like we have here,

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.230
or you can also get them
with cheese and bacon.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.446
And then finally, again,

00:08:30.446 --> 00:08:32.121
surprising you don't have these in the US,

00:08:32.121 --> 00:08:33.260
these are some jalapeño poppers.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.413
Just kind of mini jalapeños, breaded,

00:08:35.413 --> 00:08:37.250
fried, with some cheese inside.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.920
Now, I'm super excited to try these.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.015
These are Marmite Scrolls.

00:08:41.015 --> 00:08:43.708
What it is, is kind of
pieces of dough rolled up

00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:46.540
with some cheese and some
Marmite in the middle of them.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.173
Now, Joe, if you've never had Marmite,

00:08:48.173 --> 00:08:49.752
it sounds gross, 'cause it's actually --

00:08:49.752 --> 00:08:52.520
Joe: Harry, yes, I actually
in fact have had Marmite.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.010
It was a while ago in college.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.880
I lived briefly with a British
guy, he had a jar of it.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.090
I did try it once.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:00.660
I don't remember exactly how it tasted,

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.570
but I do recall comparing
it to the taste of vomit.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:04.895
So suffice to say,

00:09:04.895 --> 00:09:07.811
I'm in the "not fan of Marmite" category.

00:09:07.811 --> 00:09:11.720
So far, the Papa John's
sides game is pretty strong.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:12.953
Now, for wings,

00:09:12.953 --> 00:09:16.553
we have a honey chipotle wing sauce.

00:09:16.553 --> 00:09:18.303
Garlic knots.

00:09:18.303 --> 00:09:19.861
Oh, man!

00:09:19.861 --> 00:09:21.570
Ugh!

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:25.310
Dude, this thing is
drenched in their butter.

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:27.890
I'm confused by this next USA-only thing.

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.610
It is called a Papadia.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.040
I mean, it's a calzone,
but for some reason

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.180
they're calling it a Papadia,

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.405
which I assume is a playoff of quesadilla.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.530
Yeah, look, it's just a pizza

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.530
that they cut and folded over, right?

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.520
Moving on! These look good.
[hands slapping]

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.710
These look right up my alley.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.810
These are the jalapeño
popper rolls and ranch.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.060
Forgot, we also got breadsticks!

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.385
Here are some US-exclusive sauces:

00:09:55.385 --> 00:09:56.493
spicy garlic,

00:09:56.493 --> 00:09:58.318
ranch, of course,

00:09:58.318 --> 00:10:00.026
honey mustard,

00:10:00.026 --> 00:10:01.759
blue cheese,

00:10:01.759 --> 00:10:03.510
regular cheese.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:07.370
And you can also get, big surprise,

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.180
a side of banana peppers.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.286
Also, side of jalapeños.

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:14.860
And I was as surprised as anyone to see,

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:18.260
also in the US, you can get these.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.301
Side of anchovies.

00:10:20.301 --> 00:10:21.440
[bell dings]

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.870
Harry: Finally, for those
of you with a sweet tooth,

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:25.510
Papa John's in the UK has
a few exclusive desserts.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:28.190
Sides, we have some chocolate
scrolls on my right,

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.360
and some cinnamon scrolls on my left.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.820
And then finally we have
some Ben and Jerry's.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.130
Papa John's in the UK is kind of like

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.560
a Ben and Jerry's licensed
vendor, which is quite cool.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.830
And then also we can get
some milkshakes here,

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.870
which are a brand called F'real,

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:41.945
and they're not bad.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.790
Joe: And for dessert, the one thing we got

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.148
that you don't have, UK,

00:10:47.148 --> 00:10:48.940
cinnamon pull-aparts.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.860
Again, apologies. It's
been sitting for a while.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:52.935
Dude,

00:10:54.176 --> 00:10:55.284
yes to these.

00:10:55.284 --> 00:10:56.277
I guess I'm not supposed to,

